-- PR-MERGE-SLA-10M-1 closeout (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000291). Owner directive 2026-10-26: every pull request merges within 10 minutes of opening.
-- WHAT WAS STALE: the lever text of the pr_open_over_10m trigger and the auto_fix text of the queue_sla row pr-open-over-10m were written for fleet-control 0.49.0. Since then 0.49.3 counts a
--   pull request an author holds, or a .github/ change while the lane is not allowed to merge it, apart from the headline (waits_on, held_over_10m, session_over_10m), and 0.50.0 (OWNER-AUTO-APPROVE-ALL-1)
--   lets the lane merge a .github/ change unless ops_config stale_pr_merge_workflows is off. The issue this trigger files would have sent its reader to a query that lists held rows and to a rule that no
--   longer holds. Text only: no threshold, switch, view or schedule changes.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE analytics_metric_triggers SET action = 'Pillar autonomy (owner directive 2026-10-26: every pull request merges within 10 minutes of opening). Read them: SELECT pr, head_ref, draft, opened_at FROM pr_sla_state WHERE state = ''open'' AND last_seen >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'') AND (julianday(''now'') - julianday(opened_at)) * 1440 > 10; then the lane''s reason for each: SELECT pr, action, why, ts FROM branch_hygiene_log WHERE pr IN (...) ORDER BY id DESC. Levers by reason: a red required check is the author''s or the code loop''s to fix (the lane names the check); a conflict is conflict-repair.yml''s (scripts/conflict_repair.py), and a conflict it will not take (not a VERSION or mirror line) is the author''s; a WIP or hold marker is deliberate, so remove the marker or close the pull request; "no event" with no poke row in cloud_ops_events kind gh-poke means lane-poke.yml did not fire. Close when over_10m = 0.' WHERE metric_key = 'pr_open_over_10m'; UPDATE queue_sla SET auto_fix = 'qnfo-fleet-control branchHygieneTick (lane) and codeMergeTick merge a green, quiet pull request, a draft included (marked ready first), on the 10-minute cron and within a minute of a poke (POST /gh/poke from lane-poke.yml); .github/workflows/conflict-repair.yml merges main into a conflicted head; a red required check is the code loop''s and the author''s to fix, and the lane''s refusal names it in branch_hygiene_log. Revert: ops_config stale_pr_merge_drafts = off, stale_pr_merge_idle_min = 10.' WHERE stuck_type = 'pr-open-over-10m';
-- spof-review: no new cron, binding, credential or trigger.

UPDATE analytics_metric_triggers SET action = 'Pillar autonomy (owner directive 2026-10-26: every pull request merges within 10 minutes of opening). Read them: SELECT pr, head_ref, draft, opened_at, waits_on FROM pr_sla_state WHERE state = ''open'' AND waits_on IS NULL AND last_seen >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'') AND (julianday(''now'') - julianday(opened_at)) * 1440 > 10; then the lane''s reason for each: SELECT pr, action, why, ts FROM branch_hygiene_log WHERE pr IN (...) ORDER BY id DESC. This count leaves out what a person asked the fleet to leave: waits_on hold (an explicit request in the title, a label, the body or a HOLD: comment) and waits_on session (a change to .github/ while ops_config stale_pr_merge_workflows is off) are counted apart in v_pr_merge_sla (held_over_10m, session_over_10m). Levers by reason: a red required check is the author''s or the code loop''s to fix (the lane names the check); a conflict is conflict-repair.yml''s (scripts/conflict_repair.py: unheld drafts included, 3 minutes of quiet, git merge-tree when GitHub has not computed it), and one it refuses as needing judgement belongs to the author''s session; checks that started when the lane marked a draft ready finish first, then the next poke merges it; no gh-poke row in cloud_ops_events for the event means lane-poke.yml did not fire. Close when over_10m = 0.'
  WHERE metric_key = 'pr_open_over_10m';

UPDATE queue_sla SET auto_fix = 'qnfo-fleet-control branchHygieneTick (lane) and codeMergeTick merge a green, quiet pull request on the 10-minute cron and within a minute of a poke (POST /gh/poke from lane-poke.yml on a PR open, ready, edit, a person''s comment and a check completion): a draft is marked ready first, and since 0.50.0 a change to .github/ is merged too; .github/workflows/conflict-repair.yml merges main into a conflicted head, an unheld draft included, and decides an uncomputed mergeability with git merge-tree; a red required check is the code loop''s and the author''s to fix, and the lane''s refusal names it in branch_hygiene_log. Revert: ops_config stale_pr_merge_drafts = off, stale_pr_merge_workflows = off, stale_pr_merge_idle_min = 10.'
  WHERE stuck_type = 'pr-open-over-10m';
